# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, build with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out

# Go fuzzing corpus entries are deliberately NOT ignored. An input that fails is
# worth keeping as a regression seed, which is why CI uploads them as artifacts.
# If protocol/testdata/fuzz/ appears, commit it.

# TinyGo firmware artefacts
*.uf2
*.elf
*.hex

# Compiled interoperability clients. The sources in interop/ are tracked; the
# binaries built from them are not.
interop/libhislip_client
interop/hslclient

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# KiCad, once hardware/ exists.
#
# The rule is that anything KiCad regenerates from the schematic or board is
# ignored, and anything a human authored is tracked. Custom symbol and footprint
# libraries are authored and must be committed: a schematic that references a
# symbol nobody else has is not reproducible.
*.kicad_prl
*-backups/
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
_autosave-*
fp-info-cache
~*.lck

# Generated manufacturing and review outputs. Keep these out of the history and
# regenerate them with kicad-cli, so that the schematic remains the single source
# of truth and a stale Gerber cannot be mistaken for the current one.
hardware/output/
hardware/gerbers/
*.gbr
*.drl

# easyeda2kicad API response cache. Regenerated on demand; the generated symbol
# and footprint libraries under hardware/lib/ are what must be tracked.
.easyeda_cache/

# Local working notes, not part of the deliverable. The session handover lives
# here so that it can be candid about unfinished work without that becoming part
# of the project's public record.
*.local.md
HANDOVER*.md

# Generated netlist export. `kicad-cli sch export netlist` writes this and
# scripts/netlist-check.py consumes it; the schematic is the source of truth, so a
# checked-in netlist could only ever go stale and disagree with it.
build/

# Schematic renders produced by kicad-cli / Konnect for review. Regenerate rather
# than commit, for the same reason as the Gerbers above.
hardware/*.png
hardware/*.svg

# VSCode "Local History" extension working directory. It shadows every sheet on
# each save and contains its own nested .git, which would otherwise be committed
# as a gitlink and confuse anyone who cloned this.
.history/

# 3D models (.step/.wrl). Deliberately NOT tracked: they are ~57 MB of
# third-party mechanical assets, and git history is append-only, so committing
# them is effectively irreversible. Nothing in the netlist or the ERC gate depends
# on them; they matter for enclosure fit and for measuring part height (the
# DP9900LPB 8.0 mm figure in netlist-spec.md 4.1 came from its model).
#
# To restore them:
#   easyeda2kicad --full --lcsc_id=<C-number> --output hardware/lib/adapter
#     for each C-number in netlist-spec.md 4.3, and
#   re-clone the GPIB library at the commit in
#     hardware/lib/third-party/gpib-kicad-library/UPSTREAM_COMMIT
# Drop these two lines if you would rather carry them in-tree.
hardware/lib/adapter.3dshapes/
hardware/lib/third-party/gpib-kicad-library/3dmodels/

# Local scratch backup of the Revision 2 spec, superseded by git history
.gotmc-hislip-poe-gpib-design-spec-rev2.bak

# Repository backup bundles
*.bundle

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
